--- a parameter handed `[]` where a truth was meant, turned over, is read
--- as a mask, and the mask decided on is refused before the program
--- runs, in both modes: compiled, `not every` of a list of nothing had
--- been `!` of a list of text, which did not build (crow check --self,
--- magpie.merge's `merge_files` handed `[]` for `every`)
fn pick[xs, every]
    dedup = not every and len[xs] gt 0
    if dedup
        return 1
    return 0

log[pick[['a'], []]]
